  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1: Dry conditions through midweek, with rain \nchances late week and into the weekend.\n\nStrong high pressure firmly in place today, and it will \ncontinue to bring dry weather through at least Wednesday. \nRidging will begin to breakdown by Thursday and weak upper \ndisturbances will round the top of the ridge. This will begin to\nintroduce a daily chance for scattered afternoon rain/storms \nthrough the weekend and into early next week. Overall, severe\nthreat remains low given lack of shear to support organized\nconvection.\n\nTemperatures will gradually increase as the week progresses,\nalong with increasing humidity as return flow is introduced \nback into the region. Mid/upper 80s to low/mid 90s by the end of\nthe week and into the weekend. Overnight lows in the 50s the\nnext few nights will become more mild by end of the week with\nlows in the 60s.",
